.\" Manpage for localed
.TH LOCALED 8 "November 2026" "localed" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
localed \- D-Bus locale and keyboard management daemon for non-systemd Linux systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/libexec/localed
.RB [ \-\-replace ] [ \-\-verbose ] [ \-\-debug ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B localed
is a standalone system daemon that implements the
.B org.freedesktop.locale1
D-Bus interface using direct D-Bus activation, with no dependency on
.IR systemd .
It exposes the same locale and keyboard properties as
.BR systemd-localed (8)
on systemd-based distributions, allowing desktop tools such as
.B gnome-control-center
to read and edit the system locale and keyboard configuration on
systems that use a D-Bus/PolKit stack without systemd.
Neither elogind nor desktop-specific services are required.
.PP
.B localed
does not poll or hold any files open for writing on its own initiative.
Instead it watches its source files with
.BR inotify (7)
and re-reads them whenever they change, regardless of who changed them
\(em the bundled
.BR localectl (1)
client, a hand edit, or any other tool. After a resync it emits
.B PropertiesChanged
on the D-Bus object for every property whose value actually changed.
.PP
.B localed
is normally started on demand by D-Bus activation when a client first
calls a method or reads a property on the
.B org.freedesktop.locale1
bus name. It can also be started manually for debugging.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose debug logging to standard error in addition to syslog.
.SH "D-BUS INTERFACE"
.B localed
registers the object
.B /org/freedesktop/locale1
on the system bus, implementing the
.B org.freedesktop.locale1
interface.
.SS Properties
All properties are read-only over D-Bus; values are changed via the
configuration methods described below, or by editing the underlying files directly
(see
.BR FILES ),
which
.B localed
picks up automatically via inotify.
.TP
.B Locale \fR(as)
An array of
.RB ` KEY=value '
strings describing the active locale settings.
Keys are drawn from the standard set:
.BR LANG ,
.BR LANGUAGE ,
.BR LC_CTYPE ,
.BR LC_NUMERIC ,
.BR LC_TIME ,
.BR LC_COLLATE ,
.BR LC_MONETARY ,
.BR LC_MESSAGES ,
.BR LC_PAPER ,
.BR LC_NAME ,
.BR LC_ADDRESS ,
.BR LC_TELEPHONE ,
.BR LC_MEASUREMENT ,
and
.BR LC_IDENTIFICATION .
Only keys with non-empty values are included in the array; absent keys
are not emitted as empty strings. Values are read from
.I /etc/profile.d/lang.sh
using Slackware's shell-script format (see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.B VConsoleKeymap \fR(s)
The primary virtual console keymap name, read from the
.B KEYMAP
key in
.IR /etc/rc.d/rc.keymap .
.TP
.B VConsoleKeymapToggle \fR(s)
The secondary (toggle) console keymap, read from the sidecar file
.IR /etc/rc.d/rc.keymap.toggle .
May be empty.
.TP
.B X11Layout \fR(s)
The XkbLayout string (e.g.
.RB ` us ',
.RB ` de ',
.RB ` gb,us ')
read from the Xorg InputClass config file (see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.B X11Model \fR(s)
The XkbModel string (e.g.
.RB ` pc105 ').
.TP
.B X11Variant \fR(s)
The XkbVariant string (e.g.
.RB ` intl '
or
.RB ` nodeadkeys ').
May be empty.
.TP
.B X11Options \fR(s)
The XkbOptions string (e.g.
.RB ` terminate:ctrl_alt_bksp,compose:ralt ').
May be empty.
.SS Methods
.TP
.B SetLocale(as locale, b interactive)
Merges the supplied nonempty locale assignments with the existing system
locale. The daemon derives LANGUAGE from an incoming LANG when applicable
and removes redundant variables equal to LANG, matching systemd v262
merge and simplification behavior.
A single bare locale is interpreted as LANG. Unknown or duplicate keys
and empty or syntactically invalid values cause the entire call to fail.
Requested locale names must be installed (C and POSIX are always valid).
Locale availability is checked without changing the daemon's process locale;
locales are not generated automatically.
Both Slackware scripts are updated transactionally. Use UpdateLocale for
explicit removal or LANGUAGE priority lists.
Requires the
.B org.freedesktop.locale1.set-locale
PolKit action.
.TP
.B UpdateLocale(as locale, b interactive)
Localed extension to change only explicitly named locale assignments.
Omitted variables remain unchanged. Empty values remove the named
assignment from both shell scripts. Invalid, duplicate or empty requests
are rejected. Nonempty locale assignments must name installed locales,
except LANGUAGE, whose colon-separated translation preferences are
checked for valid syntax without requiring installed glibc locales.
Requires the same PolKit action as SetLocale.
.TP
.B SetVConsoleKeyboard(s keymap, s keymap_toggle, b convert, b interactive)
Writes
.I keymap
and
.I keymap_toggle
to
.IR /etc/rc.d/rc.keymap .
When
.I convert
is
.B true
and
.I keymap
is non-empty, a matching X11 layout is derived from the built-in
conversion table and written to the Xorg keyboard config file. The
conversion is best-effort; if no mapping exists for
.IR keymap ,
the X11 file is left unmodified. Requires the
.B org.freedesktop.locale1.set-keyboard
PolKit action.
.TP
.B SetX11Keyboard(s layout, s model, s variant, s options, b convert, b interactive)
Writes the Xorg
.IR InputClass
keyboard stanza (XkbLayout, XkbModel, XkbVariant, XkbOptions) to the
keyboard config file. The daemon parses the
.B system-keyboard
InputClass when reading the file and validates each XKB field before
exposing it through D-Bus or accepting an update. When
.I convert
is
.B true
and
.I layout
is non-empty, a matching console keymap is derived from the built-in
conversion table and written to
.IR /etc/rc.d/rc.keymap .
Requires the
.B org.freedesktop.locale1.set-keyboard
PolKit action.
.PP
For every method that takes an
.I interactive
argument, a value of
.B true
indicates the caller is willing to wait for a PolKit authentication
dialog; a value of
.B false
means the call fails immediately with
.B org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.AuthFailed
unless the caller is already authorised.
.SH AUTHORIZATION
Access to the configuration methods over D-Bus is controlled by
.BR polkit (8)
using the following actions, declared in
.IR /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.freedesktop.locale1.policy :
.TP
.B org.freedesktop.locale1.set-locale
.TQ
.B org.freedesktop.locale1.set-keyboard
.PP
The policy defaults require
.B auth_admin
for inactive or remote callers and
.B auth_admin_keep
for an active local session. A PolKit rule installed at
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/org.freedesktop.locale1.rules
additionally grants unconditional access to members of the privileged
group selected at build time (default
.RB ` wheel ',
see the
.B privileged-group
meson option), so desktop session tools are not prompted for a password
on every locale or keyboard change. Group membership changes only take
effect for new login sessions.
.PP
These PolKit actions govern D-Bus callers, including the bundled
.BR localectl (1)
client. Its set commands call the locale1 D-Bus methods with
.I interactive=true
so an authentication agent may prompt when required. Its status command
reads D-Bus properties; its list commands enumerate locally installed
locale and keyboard data and do not change system configuration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/profile.d/lang.sh
Slackware login locale script containing exported locale variables
(e.g.\n.BR "export LANG=\"en_US.UTF-8\"" ). Read for the
.B Locale
property and written atomically by
.BR SetLocale " and " UpdateLocale .
Watched with
.BR inotify (7).
.TP
.I /etc/profile.d/lang.csh
C-shell companion locale script. Updated alongside
.I lang.sh
by
.B SetLocale
and
.B UpdateLocale .
Partial updates preserve unspecified assignments in each script.
.TP
.I /etc/rc.d/rc.keymap
Slackware console keyboard script. Called by the boot process to load
the keyboard map via
.BR loadkeys (1).
.B localed
parses the
.B loadkeys
argument for the
.B VConsoleKeymap
property and regenerates the script atomically when
.B SetVConsoleKeyboard
is called. Watched with
.BR inotify (7).
.TP
.I /etc/rc.d/rc.keymap.toggle
Sidecar file persisting
.B VConsoleKeymapToggle
across reboots. Contains the bare keymap name on a single line.
Absent when no toggle keymap is configured.
Created and managed exclusively by
.BR localed .
Slackware has no native toggle-keymap concept.
.TP
.I /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/00-keyboard.conf
Xorg
.I InputClass
stanza describing the X11 keyboard layout. Written in the canonical
format used by
.BR systemd-localed (8)
so Xorg picks it up on next start. Watched with
.BR inotify (7).
The directory is created automatically if it does not exist when
.B SetX11Keyboard
is called.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.freedesktop.locale1.policy
PolKit action declarations and default authorization requirements.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/org.freedesktop.locale1.rules
PolKit rule granting the configured privileged group unconditional
access to both locale1 actions.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR localectl (1),
.BR polkit (8),
.BR pkcheck (1),
.BR inotify (7)
